From 210ce76d193c4e61a62c768159ecc610ee9db313 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Philip B. Krogh" <71797726+phibkro@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:24:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] XOpenDevice: retain the requested ID across the reply wait

_XReply may release the display lock while waiting for the server. Another thread can then reuse the output request buffer before XOpenDevice reads req->deviceid. Preserve the caller-supplied ID instead of reading the potentially overwritten request.

A real two-thread Xvfb reproducer requests device 4 while a second thread sends XNoOp requests on the same display. The unpatched library returns device 127; the patched library completes 50000 open/close cycles without an ID mismatch.
---
 src/XOpenDev.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/XOpenDev.c b/src/XOpenDev.c
index 4b3c460..0859825 100644
--- a/src/XOpenDev.c
+++ b/src/XOpenDev.c
@@ -99,7 +99,7 @@ XOpenDevice(
     if (dev) {
 	int dlen;	/* data length */
 
-	dev->device_id = req->deviceid;
+	dev->device_id = id;
 	dev->num_classes = rep.num_classes;
 	dev->classes = (XInputClassInfo *) ((char *)dev + sizeof(XDevice));
 	dlen = rep.num_classes * sizeof(xInputClassInfo);
-- 
